# Generated adapter-evaluation artifacts — never commit evaluation outputs.
#
# This list is an allowlist of names, so every NEW generated artifact has to be added
# here deliberately. An evaluation generation holds the exact held-out prompts a model
# was asked, both models' responses, and the plan-consumption ledger that records which
# dataset digests were evaluated against. All of it is reviewed locally.
#
# The bare *.jsonl rule is the backstop for the next one nobody remembers to list: the
# task pack, both arms' results and the paired comparisons are all JSONL.
evaluations/
reports/
proposals/
quarantine/
evaluation_quarantine/
configs/*.json
*.jsonl
evaluation_runs.jsonl

# Keep the directory structure, the docs and the reviewed sample config tracked.
# A generated evaluation config names a specific adapter run and a specific dataset
# digest and belongs to one operator's evaluation; the template carries only REQUIRED_
# and REPLACE-ME placeholders and is reviewed like any source file, so it is the one
# JSON here that is committed.
!README.md
!.gitignore
!configs/qwen3-0.6b-adapter-eval.json
# V69 M62 S4E. The Protocol V4 configuration is TRACKED, deliberately. Its digest is
# inside the V4 plan hash that an operator's EVAL token authorises, so a scientific
# result whose configuration lived only on one machine could never be re-derived by a
# reviewer. It names adapter runs and dataset digests -- identifiers, never task bodies.
!configs/m62-s4e-reference-pair-live.json
